# Back-end API Routes

Follow patterns in existing routes; see [backend-structure.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/backend-structure.mdc) for models and folder layout.

## Handler stack

```
authenticateToken → role/permission guard → validate(Joi) → asyncHandler → { success, data }
```

Use helpers from `middleware/errorHandler.js`: `asyncHandler`, `validationError`, `notFoundError`.

## Response envelope

```json
{ "success": true, "data": { ... }, "pagination": { ... } }
{ "success": false, "message": "...", "errors": [ ... ] }
```

- **201** on create
- Global error handler maps MySQL codes (`ER_DUP_ENTRY` → 409, JWT failures → 401)

## Validation

- Shared schemas in `middleware/validation.js` for core domains
- Route-local Joi objects for resource-specific shapes (see `companies.js`)
- Cap pagination `limit` (often max 100)

## URLs

- Kebab-case under `/api/` (e.g. `/api/company-product-stock`)
- Register new routers in `server.js`

## Auth & RBAC

From `types/user.js` — lower `roleLevel` = higher privilege:

| Level | Role |
|-------|------|
| 0 | SYSTEM_ADMIN |
| 1 | COMPANY_OWNER |
| 2 | STAFF_MEMBER |
| 3 | USER |

- `requireRole(n)` — denies when `req.user.roleLevel > n`
- Company-scoped routes: filter by `req.user.companyId` or use `requireSameCompany`
- Roles live in **`users_role`** (not deprecated `users.role`)

## System catalog `isVerified`

On system catalog POST/PUT: SYSTEM_ADMIN controls `isVerified`; COMPANY_OWNER submissions forced to `isVerified: false` on backend (see `systemServices.js`).

## Reference implementations

- `back-end/routes/companies.js` — pagination, Joi, role guards
- `back-end/routes/systemServices.js` — system catalog + isVerified
- `back-end/routes/services.js` — company services
- `back-end/middleware/auth.js`
- `back-end/middleware/errorHandler.js`

## Verification

Manual: hit new/changed endpoints with test credentials (`TESTING_CREDENTIALS.md`). Confirm envelope shape and auth failures return correct status codes.
